course: dictionary
lesson: 15587
title: Synonymous words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Synonymous words have the same or nearly the same meaning. «Big» and «large» are synonymous, so you can often swap one for the other. A thesaurus is a book or website that lists synonyms, which helps you make your writing more interesting.
explain: Synonymous is an adjective, and it is often used with the word «with». «Paris is synonymous with romance» means that when people think of Paris, they think of romance straight away, because the two are closely connected.
explain: Be careful, because some synonyms are not exactly the same. «Small» and «tiny» are close, but «tiny» is stronger. To check, swap the word into your sentence and ask yourself if it still sounds right.
explain: Some writers use the phrase «almost synonymous». «Her name is almost synonymous with kindness» means people connect her name with kindness, though the link is not quite as perfect as it would be for a true match.
fact: Synonyms are words with the same or nearly the same meaning.
fact: «Happy» and «glad» are synonyms.
fact: «Synonymous» means having the same or nearly the same meaning, or being closely linked in people's minds.
fact: «Sunshine» is synonymous with summer for many people.
fact: A thesaurus is a book that lists synonyms for words.
exercise: «Big» and «large» are almost the same in meaning. What does synonymous mean? | Found only in old dictionaries | *Having the same or nearly the same meaning | Having opposite meanings | Written in a very long way
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as «big»? | short | *large | thin | tiny
exercise: «Paris is synonymous with romance.» What does this suggest? | Paris has no romance at all | Romance is a small town near Paris | *People think of Paris and romance together | Paris is a very quiet place
test: Which two words are synonyms? | hot and cold | cat and dog | sun and moon | *quick and fast
test: «Sunshine is synonymous with summer for many people.» What does this mean? | Sunshine means the same as rain | Sunshine is a kind of winter | Summer is too hot for sunshine | *Sunshine and summer are closely connected in people's minds
exam: «Tiny» and «small» are almost synonymous. What does almost synonymous mean? | Opposite in meaning | Exactly the same in every way | *Very close in meaning, but not exactly the same | Only used in poems
